# Environment / secrets — never commit real keys (see SECURITY.md)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env.local
# .env backups written by scripts/sonar_watch.py before its rewrite — same
# secret content as .env, so the same rule: never committable.
.env.bak-*

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.streamlit/config.local.toml

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# App runtime artifacts
outputs/
logs/
*.log
usage_history.json
# Witness input: intentionally starts as a placeholder template, but its whole
# purpose is to be filled with a real witness's name, relationship, and
# observations about a real veteran — PII/PHI the moment it is real. It ships
# once as a template, then leaves version control for good.
witness.json
# VA.gov downloader failure evidence (signed-in page screenshots/HTML — PHI)
va_gov_download_artifacts
# Veteran medical records (PHI): users drop C-file PDFs in the project root to
# run scripts/ocr_records.py locally, and the OCR output is written alongside
# the input as <name>.ocr.pdf. None of it may ever be committable — `git add .`
# must not be able to stage a record, wherever in the tree it sits. A pattern
# without a slash matches by basename at any depth; the explicit `*.ocr.pdf`
# line stays last so the OCR output remains excluded even if a narrower
# `!…​.pdf` re-include is ever added below `*.pdf`.
*.pdf
*.ocr.pdf

# macOS “Save As… “ duplicates (foo.py -> “foo 2.py”) and similar stray copies
* 2.*
* 3.*

# Agiloop build harness — generated/managed per build, not part of the app
CLAUDE.md
.claude.md
.claude/
.claudeignore
.implement/
.opencode/
